    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a2e7513_1949c7ac",
        "filename": "README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T12:57:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What about inheriting the parent directory package default_visibility before falling back to this?\n\nWhat this feature gives over normal defaults inheritance is the guarantee that no modules are unintentionally missed. With a parent directory fallback that would extend to a whole directory tree, so we could e.g. put a default_visibility\u003d[\"//art:__subpackages__\"] in art/Android.bp and be assured it applies everywhere in art/ where there aren\u0027t other visibility properties.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d5e8c97_c0c6ef91",
        "filename": "README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T15:25:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s not how it works in Blaze but we already have some differences so it\u0027s not a deal breaker.\n\nLonger term we are going to switch to having private be the default. The idea is that we would do a LSC which set the default visibility in each package to legacy_private and then switch the global default to private. If the default visibility affected sub packages as well that could be quite confusing.",
      "parentUuid": "4a2e7513_1949c7ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5793b472_e82247d8",
        "filename": "README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T18:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But if the visibility is set in a package module it would override that legacy_public/legacgy_private default regardless. The only difference is whether it also applies to modules in subdirectories without their own package modules.\n\nBtw, what\u0027s your motivation for adding this? In Blaze package rules exist because that\u0027s the only way to supply defaults, however in Soong we have the defaults modules which are more elaborate. As I said, the only thing I see that this buys us is a guarantee that the visibility gets set for all modules that don\u0027t inherit a visibility through any default. I think that\u0027s pretty useful though, and it gets even more useful if it applies recursively in the directory tree.\n\n+ccross and +dwillemsen, WDYT about how this fits into the general Soong design?",
      "parentUuid": "8d5e8c97_c0c6ef91",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "075c13eb_9f53263d",
        "filename": "README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-06T15:01:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My motivation is the work on runtime module. As part of that I need to identify all the dependencies (in both directions) that cross the runtime module boundary which means I need to set the visibility for every module. Having a package level dependency makes that an easier process. More information in the bug.\n\nFalling back up the hierarchy will complicate the code (the mutators will visit packages in non deterministic order) and won\u0027t really give us any advantages for the purpose I need it.\n\nAs to how falling back fits into the general Soong design AFAIK there are no implicit dependencies between any of the .bp files whether they are ancestor/descendant or not so I think that would be unique.",
      "parentUuid": "5793b472_e82247d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46ed77f0_44be1c63",
        "filename": "README.md",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-10T13:46:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e /.../ and won\u0027t really give us any advantages for the purpose I need it.\n\nIt would for me in the use case I mentioned: I can put a package_module{default_visibility\u003d[\"//art:__subpackages__\"]} in art/Android.bp and rest assured that no one accidentally adds a new subdirectory with its own Android.bp where they simply forget to limit visibility (before the global default is changed to legacy_private).\n\nBut I\u0027m fine to descope that to a separate CL. Would be good to decide if that\u0027s the way to go though; I can take on the implementation myself.",
      "parentUuid": "075c13eb_9f53263d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 45
      },
