    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a39d8bd5_b6ea02eb",
        "filename": "android/package.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T12:57:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is all this business with the `duplicated` bool and the logic around it just to get a message that start with the package name? Isn\u0027t it overall simpler to just mention the package in the free text message instead? E.g:\n\nmodule \"\u003csome weird internal name\u003e\": Duplicate package modules in \"//top\"\n\nI think it\u0027d be good to avoid this property because it can cause uncertainty about whether duplicate packages actually are supported somehow.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa03bac5_57a4deff",
        "filename": "android/package.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T15:25:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The error message you would get would be:\n\nmodule \"soong package \u003cnon deterministic number\u003e\": Duplicate package modules in \"//top\"\n\nWhile having duplicate entries is an edge case I think that would be incredibly confusing to a developer to see a message like that.\n\nI could avoid using this field if there was a way to get hold of the scanner.Position to pass to the BaseModuleContext.Errorf(...) function but that is internal. I might be able to fake one up but the line number would be wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "a39d8bd5_b6ea02eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac402d7b_e24f15f2",
        "filename": "android/package.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T18:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Personally I\u0027d just ignore the internal module name I wouldn\u0027t recognise, and concentrate on the useful info later in the message.\n\nBut sure, it\u0027d be even better to not display the former at all. What about printing a message without the \u0027module \"foo\":\u0027 prefix? If there isn\u0027t a function for that, maybe we can add it? It\u0027d do away with a bit of complicated logic below.",
      "parentUuid": "fa03bac5_57a4deff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89cd6854_175f954a",
        "filename": "android/package.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-06T15:01:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought it better to make the code a little more complicated to avoid having to deal with lots of people asking what the weird module name was. Following the principle that code should be written to make it easy for the hundreds of end users not simpler for a few developers.\n\nThe BaseModuleContext.Errorf(...) that I mentioned in my previous comment would allow us to do exactly what you suggested however it requires a scanner.Position instance and that is not exposed outside blueprint. TBH I don\u0027t know why the Errorf(...) method exists because AFAICT it is largely useless without access to the scanner.Position of a Blueprint module.",
      "parentUuid": "ac402d7b_e24f15f2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25ba6d2d_9d2c19d7",
        "filename": "android/package.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T12:57:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can this be done in visibilityRuleGatherer instead? That would contain the visibility code in visibility.go and its own mutators, and the mutators here would be less coupled.\n\nThen I think the package mutators could be registered earlier, which seems like a good thing if other mutators need to use the package modules.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 163,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6cf15f54_69949759",
        "filename": "android/package.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T15:25:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can\u0027t be done as part of the visibilityRuleGatherer because that relies on information stored by this mutator. So, this mutator has to run before it. This mutator could store the unparsed value and then have the visibilityRuleGatherer parse it for every module but that would be doing a lot of duplicate work.\n\nI don\u0027t see why this being separate from visibilityRuleGatherer prevents it from being registered as early as possible.",
      "parentUuid": "25ba6d2d_9d2c19d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 163,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cade5a95_6b120b2e",
        "filename": "android/package.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-04T18:16:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I figured the position of registerPackageInfoGatherer fairly late in the preArch list is because the error checks in registerVisibilityRuleChecker need to happen before the parseRules calls below.\n\nYes, I was thinking just storing the plain visibility lists here. visibilityRuleChecker would check them just like in any other module, and visibilityRuleGatherer would process the package modules along with all the others and store them in visibilityRuleMap - no repeated parsing required.\n\nThe lookup of package defaults would need to be done in visibilityRuleEnforcer then. Alternatively another visibility mutator is added just before visibilityRuleGatherer to visit the package modules and populate visibilityRuleMap, so that visibilityRuleGatherer can look them up there.",
      "parentUuid": "6cf15f54_69949759",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 163,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "3f1ca97675e2f5bb8643f19ca6e04646b707d208",
